{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf clair3 [-h] [-r REGION] [--model NAME|DIR] [--gpu]\n                             [--reference-evidence {none,gvcf}] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region (e.g. chr20:1-1000000)\n  --model NAME|DIR      Clair3 model directory, or the name of a bundled model, matching the\n                        reads' basecaller (e.g. r1041_e82_400bps_sup_v500). Overrides config\n                        clair3_model; default: chosen from the basecaller metadata.\n  --gpu                 Call on Apple Silicon MPS (WGSE-built caller), or an NVIDIA GPU in HKU's\n                        Clair3 GPU image (x86-64 Linux, Docker; see docs/ont.md).\n  --reference-evidence {none,gvcf}\n                        Also write reference evidence: a gVCF, clair3.g.vcf.gz (+ .tbi), beside\n                        the unchanged variant VCF (gvcf; costs ~2.4x the time on a CPU, ~4.3x on\n                        CUDA; MPS varies), or not (none). Default: config reference_evidence, else\n                        none.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n2 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract vcf clair3 --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf clair3 --input ont.bam\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  clair3.vcf.gz (+ .tbi).\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: docker,\n  run_clair3.sh, sambamba, wgse-clair3; hours on a 30x genome.\n",
